/name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKOCHI, MASAKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A foamed chocolate which can be foamed without resort to any special apparatuses or emulsifiers, has a lightened chocolate texture and shows no oily feel. This foamed chocolate is produced by adding an oil mixture comprising an edible fat or oil with tri-saturated fatty acid glycerides containing behenic acid.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un chocolat alvéolé que l'on peut mousser sans recourir à un quelconque appareil ou émulsifiant spécial. Ledit chocolat a une texture allégée et ne présente aucune sensation huileuse. On fabrique le chocolat alvéolé en ajoutant un mélange d'huile comprenant une graisse ou huile alimentaire avec des glycérides d'acides gras tri-saturés contenant de l'acide béhénique.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>